“People who have insomnia are desperate. I treat patients who are suicidal, who have quit their jobs, whose lives are completely on hold because of their sleeping issues. And they’re vulnerable. My clients have spent hundreds and hundreds of pounds on things that made no difference. If people are being mis-sold expensive things and they’re being preyed upon, that’s a huge problem.”

Rosie Davies-Smith, a PR consultant, says she has spent more than £600 on a variety of treatments, including a combination of doctor-prescribed and over-the-counter medications, teas, supplements, weighted blankets, and eye masks. “While supplements, exercise, and sleep hygiene provided some relief, the true breakthrough came from addressing the root causes of my insomnia through therapy,” she tells me.","entities":[],"facts":[]}

{"title":"How ego and fear fuelled the rise of artificial intelligence (The Age, 2023-12-09T18:30:00+00:00)","text":"How ego and fear fuelled the rise of artificial intelligence (The Age, 2023-12-09T18:30:00+00:00)
Researchers inside OpenAI, Google and other companies thought this rapidly improving technology could be a path to AGI. But Amodei was unhappy about the Microsoft deal because he thought it was taking OpenAI in a really commercial direction. He and other researchers went to the board to try to push Altman out, according to five people familiar with the matter. After they failed, they left. Like DeepMind’s founders before them, they worried that their new corporate overlords would favour commercial interests over safety.

In 2021, the group of about 15 engineers and scientists created a new lab called Anthropic. The plan was to build AI the way the effective altruists thought it should done – with very tight controls. “There was no attempt to remove Sam Altman from OpenAI by the co-founders of Anthropic,” said an Anthropic spokesperson, Sally Aldous.","entities":["How ego and fear fuelled the rise of artificial intelligence","effective altruists","Amodei","Microsoft deal","commercial interests","Sally Aldous","group of about 15 engineers and scientists","creation of Anthropic","attempt to remove Sam Altman from OpenAI","DeepMind","Microsoft","The Age","Google","safety","Anthropic"],"facts":["How ego and fear fuelled the rise of artificial intelligence -MENTIONS-> disinformation","How ego and fear fuelled the rise of artificial intelligence -MENTIONS-> Musk","How ego and fear fuelled the rise of artificial intelligence -MENTIONS-> Page","How ego and fear fuelled the rise of artificial intelligence -MENTIONS-> Mark Zuckerberg","How ego and fear fuelled the rise of artificial intelligence -MENTIONS-> Peter Thiel"]}

